      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-250175",
      ":question/problem": "Let $V$ and $E$ be, respectively, the set of vertices and edges of a graph with $27$ edges.\nWe want to determine the sum of the degrees of all vertices in the graph.\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nEach edge in a graph has {{field-1}} incident to it. If we sum the degrees of all vertices in the graph, each edge will be counted {{field-2}}. Therefore,\n$2$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}} {{field-5}}"
